istence",[232,240,241,244],{},[235,242,243],{},"Supporting services"," — Any additional infrastructure your application depends on",[225,246,247,248,252],{},"The Docker Compose configuration lives in ",[249,250,251],"code",{},"deployment\u002Fdocker-compose\u002F"," and can be started with a single command to give you a production-like environment for local testing.",[220,254,256],{"id":255},"staging","Staging",[225,258,259],{},"The staging environment runs on Kubernetes and mirrors production as closely as possible:",[229,261,262,265,268],{},[232,263,264],{},"Kubernetes-based deployment using Helm charts",[232,266,267],{},"Separate data stores from production for safe migration testing",[232,269,270],{},"Accessible to the development team for pre-production verification",[220,272,274],{"id":273},"production","Production",[225,276,277],{},"Production is a full Kubernetes deployment managed through Helm charts:",[229,279,280,283,286,289],{},[232,281,282],{},"High-availability configuration with appropriate replica counts",[232,284,285],{},"Managed data persistence",[232,287,288],{},"TLS termination and ingress configuration",[232,290,291],{},"Monitoring and observability integration",{"title":293,"searchDepth":294,"depth":294,"links":295},"",2,[296,297,298],{"id":222,"depth":294,"text":223},{"id":255,"depth":294,"text":256},{"id":273,"depth":294,"text":274},"Development, staging, and production environment configuration.","md",null,{},{"icon":117},{"title":114,"description":299},"8xW2EoK7sTWsnftneXO7HVtZ-R_6rFkWP66EHegph5M",[307,309],{"title":109,"path":110,"stem":111,"description":308,"icon":112,"children":-1},"The Kinotic deployment pipeline from development to production.",{"title":119,"path":120,"stem":121,"description":310,"icon":6,"children":-1},"How a git push to your project's repository becomes a running deployment.",1788322990300]